## Self-Hosted Setup

This is a **self-hosted** EnvHaven workspace.

### SSH Access

Set these environment variables for correct connection strings:

| Variable | Example | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `ENVHAVEN_SSH_HOST` | `myserver.com` | External hostname |
| `ENVHAVEN_SSH_PORT` | `2222` | External SSH port (default: 2222) |

**SSH command:** `ssh abc@<host> -p 2222`

**Haven CLI:** `haven connect . abc@<host>:2222`

### Port Mapping

Map container ports in `docker-compose.yml`:

```yaml
ports:
  - "8443:8443"   # Web IDE
  - "2222:22"     # SSH
  # - "127.0.0.1:3000:3000"   # App dev server (optional; drop 127.0.0.1 to expose)
```

### Starting Dev Servers

Default apps to **port 3000** and bind `0.0.0.0`. Map that port in `docker-compose.yml`: the reference compose ships it commented out and loopback-bound (`127.0.0.1:3000:3000`), so uncomment the line and drop the `127.0.0.1` prefix to reach it from other machines. Then hand the user the link to open: `http://<your-host>:3000`. Give them the URL, not just the port.

### Cloudflare Tunnels (Optional)

`cloudflared` is included. Set `CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN` to enable automatic tunnel.

### Password Authentication

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `PASSWORD` | Web GUI password |
| `SUDO_PASSWORD` | SSH and sudo password |

See [docs/configuration.md](https://github.com/envhaven/envhaven/blob/master/docs/configuration.md) for full configuration reference.

